 "title": "MPE for Peak",
 "version": "0.15",
 "label": "MPEF Ver 108.469",
 "summary": "Per-note pitch bend, pressure (channel or poly aftertouch) and slide (MPE) on the Peak's 8 voices, a per-patch MPE switch (VOICE page) and Settings MPE pages; one or two zones. v0.2: the arpeggiator ignores its own notes when a DAW sends them back (MIDI loop). v0.3: turning a knob shows envelope times in ms and the filter cutoff in Hz, with a value bar, and Pickup shows an arrow and a distance bar. v0.4: Settings > MPE > PressCurve chooses stock's squared pressure or a linear curve. v0.5: CC 11 on a member channel works as pressure. v0.6: Settings > MPE EXTRAS > EnvSync sets the amp Decay and Release to a note length (1/2 to 1/16) at the current tempo (v0.7: a changed setting applies after 1 s). v0.8: hold Mod and move a slider or knob to put its modulation destination in the first free matrix slot; the encoder chooses the source. v0.11: Settings > PARAM LOCK keeps the FX, Arp or Voice settings through a patch change. v0.12: Settings > COPY SECTION copies an oscillator, envelope or LFO to another; Mod + Page left/right undoes and redoes the last change; Settings > MIDI MONITOR shows the last message and the DIN overflow count. v0.13: the copy and undo messages stay on screen about 2 s. v0.14: Settings > MPE EXTRAS > Glide starts a poly glide from the previous note (LastNote), or only while another note is held (Legato), instead of from the voice's own last pitch; EnvSync and undo timings corrected. v0.15: the patch's messages always clear and stay 3 s; Msg Time 127 now lasts about 3 s (stock: 1.5 s). Tested on one Peak with the automated hardware test rig and played from a LinnStrument.",
 "built": {
  "commit": "e0752058bc41",
  "definition": "patches/peak_mpe/patch.py"
 },
